  "schema:hasPart": [
    {
      "@type": "schema:WebPageElement",
      "beacon:chunkId": "article-10-1016-j-bj-2025-100828-sec1-p0",
      "beacon:sectionType": "introduction",
      "schema:text": "This introduction section from the article discusses Theileria annulata, its classification as an intracellular protozoan, its role as a tick-borne hemoparasite causing tropical theileriosis in cattle, and its ability to transform host cells by hijacking signaling pathways.\n\nTheileria annulata is an intracellular protozoan and a member of the phylum Apicomplexa . T. annulata, a tick-borne hemoparasite [1] , causes leukoproliferative diseases [2] in cattle, commonly known as tropical theileriosis. Theileria parasites have significant impacts on both animal and human welfare. Uniquely, they can transform their host cells by profoundly hijacking their signaling cascades [3] , leading to cancer-like phenotype characterized by immortalization, hyper-proliferation, and aggressive dissemination. However, dissemination can be attenuated by multiple in vitro passages [4] . Theileria parasites are recognized as master manipulators of their host cells, as reviewed in [5] . They modify host gene expression through both post-transcriptional and post-translational mechanisms to support their development [6] .",
      "schema:name": "Introduction:",
      "schema:mentions": [
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
          "schema:name": "Theileria annulata",
          "beacon:entityType": "ORGANISM"
        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
          "schema:name": "tropical theileriosis",
          "beacon:entityType": "DISEASE",
          "@id": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/DOID_3733"
        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
          "schema:name": "Apicomplexa",
          "beacon:entityType": "GENE"
        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
          "schema:name": "leukoproliferative diseases",
          "beacon:entityType": "DISEASE"
        }
      ],
      "beacon:relations": [
        {
