    {
      "@type": "schema:WebPageElement",
      "beacon:chunkId": "article-10-1016-j-bj-2025-100828-sec1-p3",
      "beacon:sectionType": "introduction",
      "schema:text": "This introduction section from Malak Haidar's 2025 article discusses the significance of m6A RNA modifications in biological processes such as DNA damage response, cell fate determination, innate immunity, and tumorigenesis, highlighting their role in cellular functions.\n\nFurthermore, m 6 A plays a crucial role in several biological operations, including the DNA damage response [16] , determination of cell fate [17] , innate immunity [18] and tumorigenesis , as reviewed in [19] . m 6 A RNA modifications are essential in numerous biological activities [20-24] . The presence and extent of RNA methylation vary across cell types, affecting specific mRNA targets, methylation intensity, and site selection. Intriguingly, m 6 A peaks can aggregate in distinct regions, serving various biological functions [25] .",
      "schema:name": "Introduction:",
      "schema:mentions": [
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
          "schema:name": "m6A",
          "beacon:entityType": "CHEMICAL",
