    {
      "@type": "schema:WebPageElement",
      "beacon:chunkId": "article-10-1016-j-bj-2025-100828-sec1-p5",
      "beacon:sectionType": "introduction",
      "schema:text": "This introduction section from Malak Haidar's 2025 BJ article explores the role of YTH domain family proteins in m6A modifications of host cell mRNA in the context of Theileria annulata infection, highlighting implications for gene expression and host-parasite dynamics.\n\nYTH domain family proteins might interact with unique subsets of m6A sites, leading to diverse gene expression outcomes [30] . Our study seeks to discern the influence of parasite infection on host cell mRNA m 6 A modifications using T. annulata -infected leukocytes. We also aim to understand the biological significance of m 6 A modifications in the parasite-host interaction dynamics. By employing transcriptome-wide high-throughput deep m 6 A-seq and the MACS2 algorithm (Model-Based Analysis of ChIP-Seq), we identified various mRNA methylation patterns. Additionally, we highlighted the unique characteristics of specific and shared methylations in the virulent phenotype induced by Theileria infection, modulating m 6 A levels through CRISPR-CAS9-mediated activation technologies.",
      "schema:name": "Introduction:",
      "schema:mentions": [
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
          "schema:name": "YTH domain family proteins",
          "beacon:entityType": "PROTEIN"
        },
