    {
      "@type": "schema:WebPageElement",
      "beacon:chunkId": "article-10-1016-j-bj-2025-100828-sec2-p0",
      "beacon:sectionType": "methods",
      "schema:text": "This Materials and Methods section from the article details the cell culture conditions for BL20, TBL20 B lymphocytes, and Ode macrophages, including the specific media components and supplements used for optimal growth.\n\nCell Culture: BL20 [31] , TBL20 B lymphocytes, and Ode macrophages [32] were cultured in RPMI 1640 medium supplemented with 2 mM l-glutamine (Lonza, cat. no. 12-702F), 10 mM Hepes (Lonza, cat. no. 17-737E), 10% heat-inactivated FBS (Gibco, cat. no. 10082147), 100 units/mL of Penicillin, 100 μg/mL of streptomycin (Lonza, cat. no. 17-602E), and 10 mM b-mercaptoethanol (Sigma-Aldrich, cat. no. M6250) BL20/TBL20. The virulent (V) hyper-disseminating Ode cell line was utilized at passages 53–71, while its attenuated (A) counterpart was at passages 309–317. Vm pertains to virulent macroschizont-infected macrophages cultivated at 41°C (instead of 37°C) for 4-6 days, inducing macroschizonts to develop into merozoites (Mero). During this period, host cell proliferation stops. For pharmacological inhibition of HIF-1α, Theileria -infected cells were treated with 100 μM of PX478 (MedKoo Biosciences) for up to 16 h.",
      "schema:name": "Materials and Methods",
      "schema:mentions": [
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
          "schema:name": "BL20",
          "beacon:entityType": "CELL_LINE",
          "@id": "https://www.cellosaurus.org/CVCL_L859"
        },
        {
