    {
      "@type": "schema:WebPageElement",
      "beacon:chunkId": "article-10-1016-j-bj-2025-100828-sec2-p2",
      "beacon:sectionType": "methods",
      "schema:text": "This Materials and Methods section from the study by Malak Haidar details the Western Blot Analysis procedure, including cell harvesting and lysis using specific buffers and protease inhibitors for evaluating epitranscriptomic hallmarks in leukocytes.\n\nError bars depict the standard error of the mean (SEM) across the three biological replicates. Western Blot Analysis: After specific treatments, cells were harvested and lysed using a buffer containing Hepes 20 mM (pH 8), NaCl 150 mM, EDTA 2 mM, Nonidet P40 1%, SDS 0.1%, Sodium deoxycholate 0.5% with protease inhibitors (Complete mini EDTA free, Roche) and phosphatase (PhosSTOP, Roche). Lysates were centrifuged at 13,000 rpm for 15 min at 4°C, collecting the supernatants. Proteins were separated using SDS-PAGE, transferred to a nitrocellulose membrane (Protran, Whatman) at 30V overnight at 4°C, and blocked with 4% skim milk for 1 h. The antibodies used were anti-HIF-1α (Abcam, ab2185), anti-METTL3 (SAB2104747, Sigma Aldrich ) and anti-actin (I-19, Santa Cruz Biotechnology).",
      "schema:name": "Materials and Methods",
      "schema:mentions": [
