    {
      "@type": "schema:WebPageElement",
      "beacon:chunkId": "article-10-1016-j-bj-2025-100828-sec2-p3",
      "beacon:sectionType": "methods",
      "schema:text": "This Materials and Methods section from the study details the antibodies used and the transient transfection process for macrophages, including the specific electroporation technique and reagents involved.\n\nThe antibodies used were anti-HIF-1α (Abcam, ab2185), anti-METTL3 (SAB2104747, Sigma Aldrich ) and anti-actin (I-19, Santa Cruz Biotechnology). Transient Transfection: Macrophages underwent electroporation using the Nucleofector system (Amaxa Biosystems). Approximately 5 x 105 cells were suspended in 100 μL of Nucleofector V solution mix (Lonza, cat. no. VCA-1003) with 2 μg of METTL3 (Santa Cruz Biotechnologies, cat. no. sc-437359-ACT). Alternatively, a negative control CRISPR activation plasmid (sc-437275) was used for nucleofection using the T-O17 program. Post-transfection, cells were reintroduced into fresh complete medium and incubated at 37°C with 5% CO 2 .",
      "schema:name": "Materials and Methods",
      "schema:mentions": [
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
          "schema:name": "HIF-1α",
          "beacon:entityType": "PROTEIN",
          "@id": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/gene/3091"
        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
          "schema:name": "METTL3",
          "beacon:entityType": "PROTEIN",
          "@id": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/gene/56339"
        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
          "schema:name": "actin",
          "beacon:entityType": "PROTEIN",
