    {
      "@type": "schema:WebPageElement",
      "beacon:chunkId": "article-10-1016-j-bj-2025-100828-sec2-p4",
      "beacon:sectionType": "methods",
      "schema:text": "This Materials and Methods section from the study details the procedures followed for cell post-transfection and the evaluation of macrophage dissemination capacity using a matrigel migration assay.\n\nPost-transfection, cells were reintroduced into fresh complete medium and incubated at 37°C with 5% CO 2 . Matrigel Chamber Assay: Ode macrophage dissemination capacity was evaluated in vitro using matrigel migration chambers. The assay was executed as per the Culturex instructions (Trevigen, cat. no. 3482-096-K). Following 24 h of incubation at 37°C, each top chamber well was rinsed once. Afterward, the top chamber was returned to the receiver plate, and 100 μL of cell dissociation solution AM was added to the lower chamber. This was followed by a 37°C incubation for 1 h with fluorescently labeled cells for dissociation from the membrane, before reading at wavelengths of 485 nm excitation and 520 nm emission.",
      "schema:name": "Materials and Methods"
    },
    {
      "@type": "schema:WebPageElement",
      "beacon:chunkId": "article-10-1016-j-bj-2025-100828-sec2-p5",
      "beacon:sectionType": "methods",
      "schema:text": "This Materials and Methods section from Malak Haidar's study details the incubation procedure for fluorescently labeled cells and outlines the RNA extraction process using the PureLink RNA Mini Kit.\n\nThis was followed by a 37°C incubation for 1 h with fluorescently labeled cells for dissociation from the membrane, before reading at wavelengths of 485 nm excitation and 520 nm emission. RNA Extraction: Cells were cultivated in triplicate at a density of 2.5 x 105 cells/ml. RNA was extracted using the PureLink RNA Mini Kit (Life Technologies, cat. no. 12183018A) as per the manufacturer's guidelines. The RNA's quality was assessed using a Bioanalyzer 2100, and quantified with Qubit (Invitrogen, cat. no. Q10210).",
      "schema:name": "Materials and Methods",
      "schema:mentions": [
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
