    {
      "@type": "schema:WebPageElement",
      "beacon:chunkId": "article-10-1016-j-bj-2025-100828-sec2-p6",
      "beacon:sectionType": "methods",
      "schema:text": "This Materials and Methods section from Malak Haidar's 2025 article details the qRT-PCR procedure used for analyzing RNA from Theileria annulata-infected leukocytes, including reagents and equipment employed for the transcription and amplification processes.\n\nQ10210). qRT-PCR: Total RNA was reverse transcribed with the High-Capacity cDNA Reverse Transcription Kit (Applied Biosystems, cat. no. 4368814). Real-time PCR involved a cDNA template, Fast SYBR Green Master Mix, and forward and reverse primers. The PCR was executed on the 7500 HT Fast Real-Time PCR System (Applied Biosystems). GAPDH served as a reference gene, and results were evaluated via the 2 −ΔΔCT method with three biological replicates.",
      "schema:name": "Materials and Methods",
      "schema:mentions": [
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
          "schema:name": "Theileria annulata",
          "beacon:entityType": "ORGANISM"
        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
          "schema:name": "GAPDH",
          "beacon:entityType": "GENE",
