        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "schema:WebPageElement",
      "beacon:chunkId": "article-10-1016-j-bj-2025-100828-sec2-p8",
      "beacon:sectionType": "methods",
      "schema:text": "This Materials and Methods section from the study by Malak Haidar describes the analysis of cell population phases and the quantification of m6A modifications in RNA from Theileria-infected leukocytes using specific software and a methylation quantification kit.\n\nCell populations in the sub-G1 (G0), G1, S, and G2/M phases were categorized and analyzed based on their DNA content using the BD FACSDiva™ Software (BD Biosciences). Quantitation of m6A Levels: m6A modifications in RNA samples from Theileria -infected leukocytes were quantified using the EpiQuik™ m6A RNA Methylation Quantification Kit (EpiGentek, P-9005-96). In this procedure, total RNA is immobilized onto strip wells using an RNA high-binding solution. The presence of m6A is identified using a specific N6-methyladenosine capture antibody followed by a detection antibody. The resulting signal is amplified and subsequently quantified colorimetrically by measuring the absorbance at a wavelength of 450 nm using a microplate spectrophotometer.",
      "schema:name": "Materials and Methods",
      "schema:mentions": [
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
          "schema:name": "Theileria",
          "beacon:entityType": "ORGANISM",
          "@id": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/Taxonomy/Browser/wwwtax.cgi?id=5873"
        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
          "schema:name": "m6A",
          "beacon:entityType": "CHEMICAL",
          "@id": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_21891"
        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
          "schema:name": "EpiQuik™ m6A RNA Methylation Quantification Kit",
          "beacon:entityType": "DRUG",
          "@id": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_18273"
        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
          "schema:name": "BD FACSDiva™ Software",
          "beacon:entityType": "CELL_LINE"
        }
      ],
      "beacon:relations": [
        {
          "@type": "beacon:Relation",
          "beacon:subject": "Theileria",
          "beacon:predicate": "associated_with",
          "beacon:object": "m6A modifications",
          "beacon:evidence": "m6A modifications in RNA samples from Theileria-infected leukocytes"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "schema:WebPageElement",
      "beacon:chunkId": "article-10-1016-j-bj-2025-100828-sec2-p9",
      "beacon:sectionType": "methods",
      "schema:text": "This Materials and Methods section from the article outlines the colorimetric quantification of signals and describes the MeRIPseq process for isolating and enriching mRNA from Theileria-infected leukocytes.\n\nThe resulting signal is amplified and subsequently quantified colorimetrically by measuring the absorbance at a wavelength of 450 nm using a microplate spectrophotometer. MeRIPseq and Data Analysis: Total RNA was isolated from Theileria -infected leukocytes and assessed for quality. mRNA was enriched using EpiQuik CUT&RUN m6A RNA Enrichment (MeRIP) Kit (EpiGentek, P-9018) as per the manufacturer’s instructions. Briefly, RNA sequences in both ends of the target m6A-containing regions are cleaved/removed, and the target m6A-containing fragments are pulled down using a beads-bound m6A capture antibody. The enriched RNA is then released, purified, and eluted. RNAseq libraries were constructed with Truseq stranded RNA LT kit (Illumina) as per the manufacturer and sequencing was performed on an Illumina HiSeq 4000 system. RNA-Seq read were trimmed with trimmomatic [33] and first mapped against the human genome (hg38) [34] using bowtie2 [35] . With the samtools and bedtools suites (PMID: 19505943; PMID: 20110278), unmapped reads were retrieved and subsequently mapped against the cow genome (Btau_4.6.1) [36] . Methylated regions were predicted with the callpeak function in macs2 ( https://github.com/macs3-project/MACS ) [37] using the immunoprecipitated and control data. Differentially expressed genes were determined from the control data using Deseq2 [38] . The raw sequencing datasets generated in this study are available in the European Nucleotide Archive (ENA) with the following accession numbers: PRJEB72277.",
      "schema:name": "Materials and Methods",
      "schema:mentions": [
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
          "schema:name": "Theileria",
          "beacon:entityType": "ORGANISM",
          "@id": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/Taxonomy/Browser/wwwtax.cgi?id=5873"
        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
          "schema:name": "EpiQuik CUT&RUN m6A RNA Enrichment",
          "beacon:entityType": "CHEMICAL",
          "@id": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_18273"
        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
          "schema:name": "EpiGentek",
          "beacon:entityType": "DRUG"
        }
      ],
      "beacon:relations": [
        {
          "@type": "beacon:Relation",
          "beacon:subject": "EpiQuik CUT&RUN m6A RNA Enrichment",
          "beacon:predicate": "uses",
          "beacon:object": "EpiGentek",
          "beacon:evidence": "EpiQuik CUT&RUN m6A RNA Enrichment (MeRIP) Kit (EpiGentek, P-9018)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "schema:WebPageElement",
      "beacon:chunkId": "article-10-1016-j-bj-2025-100828-sec2-p10",
      "beacon:sectionType": "methods",
      "schema:text": "This Materials and Methods section from the study details the availability of sequencing datasets and outlines the statistical analyses employed for data representation and comparisons among groups.\n\nThe raw sequencing datasets generated in this study are available in the European Nucleotide Archive (ENA) with the following accession numbers: PRJEB72277. Statistical analysis: Data are represented as mean values with their standard error of the mean (SEM). For comparisons involving two groups, an unpaired Student t-test was utilized. When comparing three or more groups, a one-way ANOVA was employed. A significance level of P<0.05 was established for all statistical assessments. The software used for these analyses was GraphPad Prism 9.",
      "schema:name": "Materials and Methods"
    },
    {
      "@type": "schema:WebPageElement",
      "beacon:chunkId": "article-10-1016-j-bj-2025-100828-sec3-p0",
      "beacon:sectionType": "results",
      "schema:text": "This Results section from the study outlines how T. annulata infection impacts mRNA methylation patterns in bovine host leukocytes, contributing to changes in cellular behavior such as proliferation and apoptosis resistance.\n\n### T. annulata infection alters bovine mRNA methylation in host leukocytes\n\nTheileria parasites are recognized for altering the phenotype of host leukocytes, leading to uncontrolled proliferation, apoptosis resistance, and heightened invasiveness/dissemination [39 ] . While we, along with others, have pinpointed components of the disrupted transcriptomes in Theileria -infected macrophages and B-cells [40, 41] , the capacity of the parasite to alter the mRNA methylome of its transformed host leukocyte remains unexplored.",
      "schema:name": "Results:",
      "beacon:subsectionTitle": "T. annulata infection alters bovine mRNA methylation in host leukocytes",
      "schema:mentions": [
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
          "schema:name": "T. annulata",
          "beacon:entityType": "ORGANISM"
        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
          "schema:name": "mRNA",
          "beacon:entityType": "GENE",
          "@id": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/gene/118229251"
        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
          "schema:name": "leukocytes",
          "beacon:entityType": "CELL_LINE",
          "@id": "https://www.cellosaurus.org/CVCL_M029"
        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
          "schema:name": "macrophages",
          "beacon:entityType": "CELL_LINE",
          "@id": "https://www.cellosaurus.org/CVCL_A8VR"
        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
          "schema:name": "B-cells",
          "beacon:entityType": "CELL_LINE",
          "@id": "https://www.cellosaurus.org/CVCL_B3QD"
        }
      ],
      "beacon:relations": [
        {
          "@type": "beacon:Relation",
          "beacon:subject": "T. annulata",
          "beacon:predicate": "alters",
          "beacon:object": "bovine mRNA methylation",
          "beacon:evidence": "T. annulata infection alters bovine mRNA methylation in host leukocytes."
        },
        {
