          "beacon:entityType": "CELL_LINE",
          "@id": "https://www.cellosaurus.org/CVCL_2G83"
        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
          "schema:name": "m6A",
          "beacon:entityType": "CHEMICAL",
          "@id": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_21891"
        }
      ],
      "beacon:relations": [
        {
          "@type": "beacon:Relation",
          "beacon:subject": "m6A",
          "beacon:predicate": "modifies",
          "beacon:object": "genes in BL20",
          "beacon:evidence": "genes modified by m6A in BL20 are frequently modified similarly in TBL20."
        },
        {
          "@type": "beacon:Relation",
          "beacon:subject": "m6A",
          "beacon:predicate": "modifies",
          "beacon:object": "genes in TBL20",
          "beacon:evidence": "genes modified by m6A in BL20 are frequently modified similarly in TBL20."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "schema:WebPageElement",
      "beacon:chunkId": "article-10-1016-j-bj-2025-100828-sec3-p8",
      "beacon:sectionType": "results",
      "schema:text": "This results section from the study explores the association between m6A methylation and differential gene expression in Theileria annulata-infected leukocytes, highlighting the identification of genes uniquely modified by m6A in different sample groups.\n\nThis observation aligns well with our previous approach. Subsequently, we identified genes exclusively modified by m6A in either BL20 or TBL20, but not in both. For these distinct gene sets, we plotted the ratios of expression levels between TBL20 and BL20 reference samples. As visualized in the upper left section of ( Figure. 3 B&C, genes exclusively modified by m6A in TBL20/TBL3 (depicted by the orange curve and labeled 'high m6A in TBL20/TBL3 only') manifest a noticeable skewness towards reduced TBL20/BL20 expression ratios. This has been annotated as ‘DOWN in TBL20/TBL3’ beneath the graph. However, an alternate interpretation could be an up-regulation in BL20/BL3. Conversely, genes solely modified by m6A in BL20 (represented by the blue curve) exhibited the opposing pattern. Intriguingly, this pattern suggests that genes undergoing m6A modification in TBL20/TBL3 tend to be down-regulated in TBL20/TBL3, while those modified in BL20/ BL3 mirror this down-regulation in BL20/ BL3. To quantitatively assess the differences in medians between the two distributions, we employed the Mann-Whitney U test, and the corresponding p-values have been provided on the plots for clarity. It's paramount to note that this is a broad observation, and individual genes might exhibit distinct behaviors.",
      "schema:name": "Results:",
      "beacon:subsectionTitle": "Association Between m6A Methylation and Differential Gene Expression",
      "schema:mentions": [
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
