    {
      "@type": "schema:WebPageElement",
      "beacon:chunkId": "article-10-1016-j-bj-2025-100828-sec3-p10",
      "beacon:sectionType": "results",
      "schema:text": "This Results section from the 2025 BJ article details the correlation between m6A modification levels and the proliferation of Theileria-infected leukocytes, emphasizing experimental approaches to enhance METTL3 expression through CRISPRa in virulent macrophages and TBL20 B cells.\n\nObserving that m6A levels rise in the more proliferative TBL20 B cells and decline in the arrested Vm macrophages, we postulated a correlation between m 6 A levels and host cell proliferative activity. To test this hypothesis, we overexpressed METTL3 in virulent macrophages and in infected TBL20 B cells using a CRISPR CAS9 activation (CRISPRa) system [43] . Using qRT-PCR and western blot analysis, we confirmed that transfection of Theileria -infected leukocytes with a METTL3-specific CRISPRa plasmid led to increased METTL3 expression ( Figure 4 6 A in virulent macrophages ( Figure. 4 A, right).",
      "schema:name": "Results:",
      "beacon:subsectionTitle": "m6A modification enhances the proliferation of Theileria -infected leukocytes",
      "schema:mentions": [
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
