    {
      "@type": "schema:WebPageElement",
      "beacon:chunkId": "article-10-1016-j-bj-2025-100828-sec3-p11",
      "beacon:sectionType": "results",
      "schema:text": "This Results section from the study investigates the effects of m6A modification on the proliferation of Theileria annulata-infected leukocytes, revealing that METTL3 overexpression significantly decreases their proliferation rates.\n\n4 A, right). Subsequently, we assessed the consequences of increased m 6 A modification on host cell proliferation. Proliferation rates were determined through cell counting and viability using an adenosine triphosphate (ATP) bioluminescence assay. Importantly, METTL3 overexpression resulted in a significant decrease in proliferation of both T. annulata -infected macrophages and B20 cells (TBL20) ( Figure. 4 B, left). In contrast, cells transfected with an empty CRISPRa plasmid showed no such change, highlighting the importance of m 6 A methylation in promoting host cell proliferation. The ATP bioluminescence results indicated that T. annulata -infected leukocytes, upon transfection with the METTL3 CRISPRa plasmid, displayed the same vitality compared to those transfected with the empty CRISPRa plasmid ( Figure. 5 Figure. 4 C, left & Fig. S1)).",
      "schema:name": "Results:",
      "beacon:subsectionTitle": "m6A modification enhances the proliferation of Theileria -infected leukocytes",
      "schema:mentions": [
