    {
      "@type": "schema:WebPageElement",
      "beacon:chunkId": "article-10-1016-j-bj-2025-100828-sec3-p14",
      "beacon:sectionType": "results",
      "schema:text": "This Results section from the article discusses how HIF-1α regulates m6A-RNA methylation, highlighting its role in the proliferation of Theileria-infected leukocytes under hypoxic conditions.\n\nHIF-1α also directly binds to the promoter region of YTHDF1, regulating its transcription under hypoxic conditions in hepatocellular carcinoma [54] . Considering our observations about the correlation of m 6 A RNA modification, as well as the function of HIF-1α in the proliferation of Theileria -infected leukocytes, we assumed that HIF-1α regulates the process of m 6 A RNA modification. To test this hypothesis, we first analyzed the HIF-1α levels in merozoite-producing macrophages (Vm) as well as virulent (V). We observed increased HIF-1α protein expression in Vm compared to virulent macrophages ( Figure 5 A, left).",
      "schema:name": "Results:",
