    {
      "@type": "schema:WebPageElement",
      "beacon:chunkId": "article-10-1016-j-bj-2025-100828-sec3-p16",
      "beacon:sectionType": "results",
      "schema:text": "This results section from the article discusses how m6A contributes to the proliferation and dissemination of Theileria-infected leukocytes through the modulation of membrane-anchored proteins like ADAMs involved in cellular interactions.\n\n6 6 A complex expression and thereby drives proliferative effects in Theileria -infected cells. ### m 6 A Modulates Dissemination in Theileria -Transformed Leukocytes\n\nADAMs (A Disintegrin And Metalloproteinase) are membrane-anchored proteins bearing structural similarities to snake venom disintegrins that play crucial roles in migration, adhesion, and both cell-cell and cell-matrix interactions (reviewed in [55] ). In our m6A-seq dataset, ADAM19 is found to be m6A-modified and overexpression of METTL3 in T. annulata -infected macrophages leads to its upregulation ( Figure 6 A).",
      "schema:name": "Results:",
      "beacon:subsectionTitle": "m 6 A Modulates Dissemination in Theileria -Transformed Leukocytes",
      "schema:mentions": [
        {
