    {
      "@type": "schema:WebPageElement",
      "beacon:chunkId": "article-10-1016-j-bj-2025-100828-sec4-p0",
      "beacon:sectionType": "discussion",
      "schema:text": "This discussion section from Malak Haidar's 2025 article examines how Theileria annulata influences host epigenetics, highlighting its role in cellular behavior changes and contributing to disease progression.\n\nThe impact of pathogens on host epigenetics offers invaluable insights into the complex interactions that underlie infection and disease progression. Among these, Theileria parasites, specifically transforming species such as T. annulata , excel at altering host cellular behavior. This capability is evident in pathological outcomes such as unchecked cellular proliferation and an increased resistance to apoptosis. Recent research has enriched our comprehension of the ways Theileria parasites reshape the transcriptomes of infected cells. Yet, the exploration of the epigenetic dimension — particularly T. annulata 's impact on mRNA methylation — remains a yet-to-be-unfolded area of study.",
      "schema:name": "Discussion:",
      "schema:mentions": [
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
          "schema:name": "Theileria annulata",
          "beacon:entityType": "ORGANISM"
        },
