    {
      "@type": "schema:WebPageElement",
      "beacon:chunkId": "article-10-1016-j-bj-2025-100828-sec4-p1",
      "beacon:sectionType": "discussion",
      "schema:text": "This discussion section from Malak Haidar's 2025 article explores mRNA methylation variations in Theileria annulata-infected leukocytes, highlighting unique m6A patterns in different macrophage types and their potential implications for virulence and disease progression.\n\nannulata 's impact on mRNA methylation — remains a yet-to-be-unfolded area of study. Utilizing ELISA assays revealed varying m6A levels across different T. annulata -infected cell lines. It's noteworthy that proliferation-arresting merozoite-producing macrophages exhibited unique methylation patterns compared to both proliferating virulent and attenuated macrophages. Additionally, m6A levels differ between the more proliferative Theileria -infected B cells (TBL20) and their uninfected counterparts, BL20.",
      "schema:name": "Discussion:",
      "schema:mentions": [
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
