    {
      "@type": "schema:WebPageElement",
      "beacon:chunkId": "article-10-1016-j-bj-2025-100828-sec4-p3",
      "beacon:sectionType": "discussion",
      "schema:text": "This discussion section from the study by Malak Haidar emphasizes the significance of diverse methodologies in epitranscriptomics and highlights patterns in m6A methylation's relationship with gene expression variability in Theileria annulata-infected leukocytes.\n\nThese differences underscore the importance of employing a range of methodologies in epigenetics research to achieve a comprehensive understanding. A closer examination of the relationship between m6A methylation and gene expression variability revealed compelling patterns. While comparisons between V and A infected macrophages showed no significant gene expression changes, the analyses of V vs. Vm and V vs. A presented a contrasting narrative. This data suggests a scenario where m6A modifications could influence gene expression in a context-specific manner.",
      "schema:name": "Discussion:",
      "schema:mentions": [
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
          "schema:name": "Theileria annulata",
          "beacon:entityType": "ORGANISM"
