          "beacon:entityType": "CELL_LINE",
          "@id": "https://www.cellosaurus.org/CVCL_0B29"
        }
      ],
      "beacon:relations": [
        {
          "@type": "beacon:Relation",
          "beacon:subject": "m6A",
          "beacon:predicate": "associated_with",
          "beacon:object": "gene expression variability",
          "beacon:evidence": "m6A methylation's relationship with gene expression variability"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "schema:WebPageElement",
      "beacon:chunkId": "article-10-1016-j-bj-2025-100828-sec4-p4",
      "beacon:sectionType": "discussion",
      "schema:text": "This discussion section from the article explores the implications of m6A modifications on gene expression in Theileria annulata-infected leukocytes, highlighting inconclusive results regarding correlations between m6A presence and upregulated gene expression.\n\nThis data suggests a scenario where m6A modifications could influence gene expression in a context-specific manner. Subsequent, the analysis aiming at associate m6A presence with upregulated gene expression yielded promising but inconclusive results. When examining genes enriched with m6A only in V and up-regulated in Vm, no correlation was detected. However, there was a correlation between genes that are m6A-enriched in Vm, and up-regulated in V, suggesting that methylation of genes in merozoites could result in their downregulation.",
      "schema:name": "Discussion:",
      "schema:mentions": [
