    {
      "@type": "schema:WebPageElement",
      "beacon:chunkId": "article-10-1016-j-bj-2025-100828-sec4-p5",
      "beacon:sectionType": "discussion",
      "schema:text": "This discussion section from the study examines the correlation between m6A enrichment and gene expression in Theileria annulata-infected leukocytes, highlighting significant overlaps in gene methylation patterns across different infection states.\n\nHowever, there was a correlation between genes that are m6A-enriched in Vm, and up-regulated in V, suggesting that methylation of genes in merozoites could result in their downregulation. Comparisons between BL20 and TBL20 highlighted a significant overlap in genes undergoing m6A methylation. This implies a consistent gene set that may be subject to such modifications, regardless of infection status. Delving deeper, some genes showed exclusive methylation in specific categories, pointing towards a potential role for m6A in downregulation of gene expression.",
      "schema:name": "Discussion:",
      "schema:mentions": [
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
