    {
      "@type": "schema:WebPageElement",
      "beacon:chunkId": "article-10-1016-j-bj-2025-100828-sec4-p7",
      "beacon:sectionType": "discussion",
      "schema:text": "This discussion section from Malak Haidar's article examines the regulatory role of m6A on E2F4 expression and its connection with HIF-1α in Theileria annulata-infected leukocytes, highlighting novel pathogen strategies.\n\nIt also raises questions regarding the potential regulatory influence of m6A on E2F4 expression, a crucial component of the cell cycle, suggesting a layered control mechanism. The proposed link between HIF-1α and m6A RNA methylation is indeed striking. With HIF-1α known to regulate m6A modulators, especially WTAP and YTHDF1, it introduces a novel perspective on the potential strategies’ pathogens might employ to manipulate host cells to favor growth. The convergence of epigenetic changes with hypoxic responses offers an integrated view of host-pathogen interactions, hinting at potential avenues for innovative treatments.",
      "schema:name": "Discussion:",
      "schema:mentions": [
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
          "schema:name": "m6A",
          "beacon:entityType": "CHEMICAL",
