    {
      "@type": "schema:WebPageElement",
      "beacon:chunkId": "article-10-1016-j-bj-2025-100828-sec4-p8",
      "beacon:sectionType": "discussion",
      "schema:text": "This discussion section from Malak Haidar's 2025 article explores the implications of epitranscriptomic modifications, particularly m6A on ADAM19, in relation to host-parasite interactions and potential therapeutic strategies against Theileria annulata infection.\n\nThe convergence of epigenetic changes with hypoxic responses offers an integrated view of host-pathogen interactions, hinting at potential avenues for innovative treatments. Identifying ADAM19 as m6A-modified is particularly captivating, given its critical role in cell migration and adhesion. If m6A does indeed influence ADAM19 expression, as the METTL3 overexpression suggests, then m6A could potentially shape the spread of Theileria -transformed leukocytes, thereby affecting disease progression and intensity.",
      "schema:name": "Discussion:",
      "schema:mentions": [
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
          "schema:name": "ADAM19",
          "beacon:entityType": "GENE",
          "@id": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/gene/8728"
        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
          "schema:name": "m6A",
          "beacon:entityType": "CHEMICAL",
          "@id": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_21891"
        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
          "schema:name": "Theileria annulata",
          "beacon:entityType": "ORGANISM"
        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
