    {
      "@type": "schema:WebPageElement",
      "beacon:chunkId": "article-10-1016-j-bj-2025-100828-sec4-p10",
      "beacon:sectionType": "discussion",
      "schema:text": "This discussion section from Malak Haidar's 2025 BJ article examines the complexities of translating research findings to in vivo scenarios, highlighting the role of m6A modifications in the host-parasite interaction during Theileria annulata infection.\n\nFurthermore, translating these findings to real-world, in vivo scenarios — especially given the complexities associated with the host immune response and the parasite's life cycle — is yet to be fully established. In summary, this study illuminates the multifaceted role of m6A modifications in the dynamic between host and parasite during T. annulata infection. Beyond the direct implications for tropical theileriosis, the involvement of m6A methylation as a significant factor in host-pathogen dynamics has been showcased in various studies [56, 57] . For instance, Baumgarten et al described a dynamic and extensive m6A mRNA methylation program that fine-tunes the transcriptional cascade during blood-stage development of Plasmodium falciparum [56] . Additionally, Farhat et al. highlighted m6A's function in creating transcriptional barriers in Toxoplasma gondii , especially for closely located, stage-specific genes [57] . When considered alongside these discoveries, there seems to be a possible evolutionary strategy among parasites, like T. gondii and T. annulata , in shaping the m6A landscape of host cells. This underlines the critical role of m6A in the regulation of gene expression, be it aiding parasite adaptation or shaping host-pathogen interactions. Combining insights from both T. gondii and T. annulata provides a comprehensive perspective on the function of m6A in host-pathogen dynamics, promoting a well-rounded approach for deciphering these interactions. Such an understanding could pave the way for innovative m6A-centric therapeutic solutions against various intracellular pathogens.",
      "schema:name": "Discussion:",
      "schema:mentions": [
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
          "schema:name": "m6A",
          "beacon:entityType": "CHEMICAL",
          "@id": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_21891"
        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
          "schema:name": "Theileria annulata",
          "beacon:entityType": "ORGANISM"
        },
        {
          "@type": "schema:Thing",
          "schema:name": "tropical theileriosis",
          "beacon:entityType": "DISEASE",
          "@id": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/DOID_3733"
        }
      ],
