    {
      "@type": "schema:ImageObject",
      "beacon:chunkId": "fig2",
      "schema:name": "Figure 2",
      "schema:caption": "Alteration in expression of m6A writers, readers, and erasers in T. annulata infected leukocytes. A. mRNA levels of m6A writers ( mettl3 , wtap , rbm15 ), readers ( ythdf1 & 3 , hnrnpa2b1 ), and erasers ( alkbh5 ) were measured by qPCR in Theileria -infected macrophages (A) and TBL20 and BL20 (B). *p value <0.05, **p value <0.005, ***p value <0.001.",
      "schema:text": "Figure 2: m6A writer genes mettl3, wtap, and rbm15 are upregulated in Theileria annulata-infected leukocytes with p-values <0.05, while the m6A eraser gene alkbh5 is downregulated (p < 0.005). The expression levels of m6A readers ythdf1 and ythdf3 are significantly altered in infected macrophages compared to uninfected controls. This indicates that m6A modifications are critically involved in the regulation of gene expression during Theileria infection, contributing to the parasite's virulence and the host's immune response.\n\nCaption: Alteration in expression of m6A writers, readers, and erasers in T. annulata infected leukocytes. A. mRNA levels of m6A writers ( mettl3 , wtap , rbm15 ), readers ( ythdf1 & 3 , hnrnpa2b1 ), and erasers ( alkbh5 ) were measured by qPCR in Theileria -infected macrophages (A) and TBL20 and BL20 (B). *p value <0.05, **p value <0.005, ***p value <0.001.",
